stty - display or change console settings

SYNOPSIS
    stty [-a]
    stty size
    stty setting ...

DESCRIPTION
    Read or change the terminal on standard input. With no operands or
    with -a, print the size, flags and control characters. The size command
    prints the row and column counts.

    Use echo, icanon, isig, iexten, icrnl or ixon to enable a setting.
    Prefix a flag with - to disable it. The sane setting restores the
    default input settings. The raw setting disables line editing, echo,
    input translation, signal keys and software flow control.

    Set a control character with its name and a value. The names are
    intr, quit, susp, eof, erase, kill, werase, rprnt, lnext, stop and
    start. Values may be literal characters, decimal bytes, caret
    notation such as '^C' or '^?', or undef to disable the character.

    Use rows number and columns number to set the pager viewport.
    The framebuffer bounds come from its detected geometry.
    The VGA text console supports 80 columns and 24 rows.

EXAMPLES
    stty size
    stty rows 20 columns 72
    stty intr '^X'
    stty sane

    After stty raw, type stty sane followed by Ctrl+J if the serial
    terminal sends carriage return when Enter is pressed.

EXIT STATUS
    The exit status is 0 on success, 1 on a terminal error, or 2 for
    invalid settings or usage.

SEE ALSO
    man(1), sh(1), ioctl(2), termios(2)
